Real-Time Application Architecture on Kubernetes with AWS RDS

This diagram explains a production-ready microservices architecture using Kubernetes and AWS RDS.

- Users access the application through a LoadBalancer
- Frontend and Backend applications run as scalable Kubernetes Pods
- ClusterIP enables secure internal pod-to-pod communication
- Backend services connect securely to AWS RDS over VPC/SSL
- AWS RDS handles database replication, backups, failover, and high availability automatically
